s":7361.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":512.0,"requests":1}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a plan-body paragraph describing why A6-0c's harness simulates a concurrent review-bot writer push (to rehearse the lease-failure precondition that A6-1 relies on) so the last three ACs map to described work.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T9"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ACs: 'In temporary real clones rooted at the rewritten branch, the harness appends and pushes one representative review-bot ticket event', 'git merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip> <new-tip> exits nonzero', 'The representative writer push increases incremental size-pack by less than 1 MB'","Body 'Publication boundary' only mentions lease failure conceptually and assigns publication to A6-1; it does not describe the harness performing a synthetic writer push"],"finding":"The final three acceptance criteria (representative review-bot ticket append/push, `merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip> <new-tip>` exits nonzero after the synthetic writer push, and incremental `size-pack` < 1 MB) have no covering description in the plan body. The Publication boundary section discusses force-with-lease and lease failure abstractly, but never states that A6-0c's harness itself simulates a concurrent writer push on the rewritten branch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2f470cb70f6a8785","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (last three lines) vs plan body","norm_id":"nfbb7d7c77fbefebc","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An implementer reads the body, builds the dry-run/assert harness, and is surprised by three ACs requiring a full temporary-clone writer-push simulation not motivated anywhere in prose."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the Publication boundary or Why-stock section, add: 'The dry-run harness also proves the lease precondition A6-1 depends on by appending and pushing one representative review-bot ticket event into a temporary clone of the rewritten branch, then asserting old-tip is no longer an ancestor and that the writer push adds <1 MB to size-pack.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","verify command `grep` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly whether the dynamic re-add is an amend of the imported tip commit (count preserved) or an appended commit (count+1), and reconcile that choice with AC-1's commit-count-equality assertion.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the rewritten HEAD tree byte-identical after the dynamic re-add'","AC-1: 'the rewritten branch commit count equals the measured old-tip commit count'","AC-4: 'After dynamic re-add, rev-parse <new-tip>^{tree} exactly equals rev-parse <old-tip>^{tree}'","The re-add restores four .bridge_state/ files that the filter stripped from every revision, so it must add tree content back at the tip — but the plan never states whether this is a fresh commit (count+1) or an amend of the imported tip (count preserved)."],"finding":"The plan asserts both that the rewritten commit count equals the old-tip commit count (AC-1) and that the rewritten HEAD tree is byte-identical to old-tip after a 'dynamic re-add' (AC-4), but never specifies whether the dynamic re-add is a new commit appended on top of the imported tip or an amend/replacement of the imported tip commit. If it is a new commit, the count becomes old-tip+1 and AC-1 fails; if it is an amend, the plan must say so and describe how the tip's parent/topology is preserved.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c5b6f66f992a61a","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"§Why stock plumbing / Required corrections item 3 / AC-1 and AC-4","norm_id":"n44fb022c1e39d754","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Implementer appends a re-add commit to satisfy tree-identity, then AC-1's commit-count-equality assertion fails on the scratch clone.","Implementer amends the tip to satisfy AC-1 but the topology/parent handling is unspecified, risking a divergent tip shape."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Specify the re-add as an in-place amend of the imported tip commit (reusing its message, author, and single/merge parent set) so the tree becomes byte-identical to old-tip while the total commit count and merge-commit count remain equal to old-tip; note this explicitly next to AC-1 and AC-4.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan asserts a <=150 MB pack-size acceptance criterion for a fresh unfiltered clone of the rewritten branch, but never accounts for the remote tag `pre-heal-a118-20260710T005736Z` that the plan's own cited session log (1cb6-d553-6565-49b4, item [3]) says pins 22,317 commits / 63 MB and 'MUST be deleted or the reclaim lands at 167 MB not 94 MiB'. A scratch clone that still fetches that tag's reachable objects would exceed the ceiling, so the asserted pack-size capability is not achievable as described without a stated tag-removal/exclusion step.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7d5f7281cd9a941e","impact